# Your own brain. install.sh copies CLAUDE.md.template here and it becomes
# personal from the first edit. The template itself stays tracked.
CLAUDE.md

# Generated outputs (personal data)
_temp/
_output/
brain/

# Personal knowledge base (your actual work data)
# These folders exist in the repo for structure, but your real content stays local
Clients/*/meetings/*.md
Clients/*/strategy/*.md
Clients/*/Research/*.md
Clients/*/*/*.md
journal/todo_*.md

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/

# Atomic-write scratch files. Every writer under journal/state/ writes `x.tmp`
# then os.replace()s it into place, so a .tmp file exists for microseconds and is
# never content anyone wants committed. Un-ignored, a sync that ran while one of
# them was in flight died with "git add failed: unable to stat ... .tmp" and left
# the whole turn's ledger change uncommitted.
*.tmp

# Runtime lock files. Process-local, meaningless in another checkout, and a
# committed one makes flock behave unpredictably for whoever clones it.
journal/state/.locks/
